    "date_str": "2025-09-03",
    "description": "Installation of Barricade Nets in selected perennial reservoirs to protect freshwater fish harvest",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.cabinetoffice.gov.lk/cab/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=16&Itemid=49&lang=en&dID=13386",
    "lang": "en",
    "decision_details_title": "Press briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)",
    "decision_details_body": "- Inland fisheries and aquaculture play a major role in providing nutritious food to the communities in rural areas. However, the washing away of fish during overflows of inland reservoirs and release of water through sluice gates has severely reduced the yield of freshwater fish. It has been identified that between 20,000 to 40,000 kilograms of fish are lost from a single freshwater reservoir per year prior to human consumption. It has been shown that washing away of mature fish leads to a decrease in fish population and the rapid depletion of future fish stocks due to the escape of sexually mature fish with breeding capacity. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Fisheries, Aquatic and Ocean Resources to implement a programme to install barricade nets in 250 selected perennial freshwater reservoirs within 02 years by the Sri Lanka National Aquaculture Development Authority in order to prevent the loss of freshwater fish harvest and to increase freshwater fish production, was approved by the Cabinet.",
    "chunk_id": "2025-09-03-007-en-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "5e4d5d4b30b950cdbd1da07e47feded6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1228,
    "chunk_text": "Installation of Barricade Nets in selected perennial reservoirs to protect freshwater fish harvest\n\nPress briefing of Cabinet Decision taken on 2025-09-03 (Subject to Confirmation at the next Meeting)\n\n- Inland fisheries and aquaculture play a major role in providing nutritious food to the communities in rural areas. However, the washing away of fish during overflows of inland reservoirs and release of water through sluice gates has severely reduced the yield of freshwater fish. It has been identified that between 20,000 to 40,000 kilograms of fish are lost from a single freshwater reservoir per year prior to human consumption. It has been shown that washing away of mature fish leads to a decrease in fish population and the rapid depletion of future fish stocks due to the escape of sexually mature fish with breeding capacity. Therefore, the proposal made by the Minister of Fisheries, Aquatic and Ocean Resources to implement a programme to install barricade nets in 250 selected perennial freshwater reservoirs within 02 years by the Sri Lanka National Aquaculture Development Authority in order to prevent the loss of freshwater fish harvest and to increase freshwater fish production, was approved by the Cabinet."
  },
